        "description": "Resembles an IDOR: the route takes a caller-supplied path parameter job_id and returns the corresponding job, which scanners commonly flag as a user-controlled resource id without an ownership check. It is actually safe because the lookup goes through authz.load_job_for_view(db, user, job_id), which calls can_view_job() and enforces role/region/customer/worker ownership scoping (authz.py:65-69, 37-46), returning 404 if the authenticated user is not entitled to the job. The serializer job_out is also called with the real user, so no over-exposure."
