        "description": "Resembles path traversal / unsafe filename handling: it derives a filename from a caller-supplied name and looks like it feeds filesystem writes, which scanners flag for CWE-22. It is actually safe because it whitelists characters (only alphanumerics plus - _ . and space are kept), strips the rest, truncates to 120 chars, and falls back to 'upload.bin' when empty \u2014 so '/', '\\\\', and '..' sequences cannot survive (e.g. '../../etc/passwd' collapses to '....etcpasswd'). No directory separators can pass through, preventing traversal."
